    {
      "id": "claim_6b5fcacdff844c2abce61736313674fb",
      "statement": "A runner task is an infinite loop: refresh liveness with `note_worker`, call `store.claim_next(worker_id)`, sleep `worker_poll_seconds` and retry when the queue is empty, otherwise `await self._run(wiki)` — so each runner holds at most one wiki at a time because `_run` does not return until that row is terminal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/worker/loop.py#L69-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57e7387bf035171dc9e11066471e7d35cf1e24f429dcbc09cc4ee84eff165513:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_686b0e280b594736943edfdaa1820abd",
      "statement": "A worker process runs the same `WorkerLoop` in two modes: `python -m app.worker` builds `Settings`+`JobStore` and runs `asyncio.run(_serve(worker))` with `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` handlers driving `worker.stop()`, while `RUN_LOCAL_WORKER=true` makes the `create_app()` lifespan start the worker in-process and stop it with the reaper in a `finally`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/main.py#L53-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5d5e0ab27eb481c512218f615ac4f9623140ea2e5cfc24f8ad661ae6877982e:"
