    {
      "id": "claim_730df6969a8c4cdc95b6d447350b478a",
      "statement": "`WorkerLoop._track` is an independent task that sleeps `WORKER_PROGRESS_SECONDS` per iteration, reads OpenWiki's durable run state from `store.repo_dir(wiki_id)` through `asyncio.to_thread(read_run_state, ...)`, logs the plan once (`openwiki plan: <total> pages planned, phase=<phase>`), computes the progress text, and calls `store.heartbeat(wiki_id, claim_id, progress=text)` on every iteration even when the text is unchanged, because the heartbeat is what refreshes the lease.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/storage.py#L271-L308",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c0451c6dd807cded94d8ca706ded480fd6d1db5ae09ef36202e437e1669ec677:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/worker/loop.py#L132-L157",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e8fc0c32d663a5670d96262684f3b351e0b87b20f4d44efefe6c18e5e28d9dd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65803f571a2b4c5e827d6a783966a498",
      "statement": "`read_run_state(repo_dir)` parses `openwiki/.run.json` into `{phase, total, completed, pending, current}` (current is the first non-complete planned page) and returns `None` on missing or unparsable JSON, tolerating a non-list `plan.pages` by reporting zeros; `format_progress(state, pages_written)` renders `\"<completed>/<total> pages\"` plus `\" · <phase>\"`, falls back to `\"<n> pages written\"`, and returns `None` when neither source has data — which is why `_track` falls back to `packer.count_pages`, counting `*.md` files under `repo/openwiki/`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/packer.py#L16-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5294b7d040656aeb3938f0eb463f2d514a9361bbbb6b126882b9411aff6decad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/wiki_runner.py#L96-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c20075e0ac1e3ccc847b85372c14e972b4c1f4078a2851a69517d79ecdcf3fb3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_wiki_state.py#L61-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d4e7dedd32378458dd0b30698ae6813d466090a3b9aadf2df3e1fbefd67d4b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8225d1eb7bf4ed6b5a131ce81068117",
      "statement": "Losing the lease is signalled through the heartbeat return value: when `heartbeat` yields `ok=False` (the `(wiki_id, claim_id)` pair no longer exists or is not in `RUNNING_STATUSES`) or `cancel=True` (the API set `cancel_requested`), `_track` sets `cancel_event` and returns, and the pipeline turns the next `report()`/`check_cancel()` into `PipelineCancelled` — `\"the worker lease was lost\"` for the first case and `\"cancelled by user\"` for the second — so the worker stops instead of writing into a row another worker now owns.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/storage.py#L280-L293",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:714a40355f1e2066e1a55a4893402e16bfa2274e72fa0e8ee25f8130bec9684e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/pipeline.py#L66-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6481ccc48c592d3a1337c1f8904627d0635a711dd36aa05e1690ed886a85b4d7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/worker/loop.py#L155-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2376f030740f8c8e8e08ca4e77120ea3584877220b9e075a99f8b25bf650a370:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e729b973436f4310a51d1dac7b287075",
      "statement": "Cancellation is cooperative and shares the progress channel: the worker exposes no cancel RPC, `_track` only observes `cancel_requested`, `cancel_event` is what makes `run_openwiki` kill the CLI child process, and `OpenWikiRunCancelled` is re-raised as `PipelineCancelled` so callers handle a single cancellation exception.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/pipeline.py#L113-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c647ed9e309e9e4e3c4df6dc657f88f3b8b3e61989494a3edf20a24b3bdaf0a:"
        },
